Optimal Solution - Layer-by-layer traversal to collect matrix elements in spiral order using boundary pointers.
                   Use four pointers to track the current layer and shrink them after each directional traversal.

class Solution {
    public List<Integer> spiralOrder(int[][] matrix) {
        // List to store elements in spiral order
        List<Integer> res = new ArrayList<>();
        // Number of rows and columns
        int n = matrix.length;
        int m = matrix[0].length;
        // Define the current boundaries of the spiral
        int left = 0, right = m - 1;
        int top = 0, bottom = n - 1;
        // Continue until all boundaries overlap
        while (top <= bottom && left <= right) {
            // Traverse the top row from left to right
            for (int i = left; i <= right; i++) {
                res.add(matrix[top][i]);
            }
            top++; // Move top boundary downward
            // Traverse the right column from top to bottom
            for (int i = top; i <= bottom; i++) {
                res.add(matrix[i][right]);
            }
            right--; // Move right boundary leftward
            // Traverse the bottom row from right to left (if valid)
            if (top <= bottom) {
                for (int i = right; i >= left; i--) {
                    res.add(matrix[bottom][i]);
                }
                bottom--; // Move bottom boundary upward
            }
            // Traverse the left column from bottom to top (if valid)
            if (left <= right) {
                for (int i = bottom; i >= top; i--) {
                    res.add(matrix[i][left]);
                }
                left++; // Move left boundary rightward
            }
        }
        // Return the spiral traversal result
        return res;
    }
}

Time Complexity :- O(N * M).
Space Complexity :- O(N * M).
